{"description":"Checks newly changed user-facing text against the plain-English house voice whenever source files under src/ are edited.","enabled":true,"name":"plain-english-check","then":{"prompt":"Check the user-facing text in the files that were just changed against .kiro/steering/plain-english.md. Flag any of the following and quote the offending text: (1) jargon used without a one-sentence plain-English glossary explanation; (2) any amount, date, or consequence that appears invented rather than entered by the user — unknown values must read as 'not entered'; (3) action lines that are not one of the fixed vocabulary: Pay / Reply / Sign and return / Show up / No action needed; (4) sentences too long or complex to pass the ten-second test. If everything complies, say so briefly. Do not rewrite the code yourself — report the findings.","type":"askAgent"},"version":"1","when":{"patterns":["src/**"],"type":"fileEdited"}}